    "created_at": "2018-07-16T21:13:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-07-16T21:13:31Z",
    "body": "Hmm, very interesting.\r\n\r\nMy point of view is that we have two issues:\r\n\r\n- The CSS spec is not clear on what properties should apply, so we don't have interoperability in what is displayed.\r\n- The HTML spec is not clear on how ::first-letter + visibility maps to innerText results.\r\n\r\nI think we should solve the second part here, so that the spec gives the same answer for innerText as a browser gives for what it displays. So the result won't be interoperable between browsers, but at least it will be consistent within browsers.\r\n\r\nMy take is that making the HTML step clear is not as much about step 2, as it is about step 4. Maybe we should say something there about how \"compute the text of the box\" takes into account any properties (like visibility) that apply to ::first-letter or ::first-line or similar? What do you think?\r\n\r\nSeparately, we could try to get interoperability on what properties apply to ::first-letter. That is probably best discussed in the CSSWG.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
