    "updated_at": "2018-07-20T04:52:28Z",
    "body": "The problem is term \"node\" in step 2. Since Text node doesn't have computed value.\r\nSo, \"step 2\" should explain where we get computed style.\r\nFor element node, it is element's computed style.\r\n\r\nHowever, for Text node, we have at most two computed style:\r\n - first-letter/fist-line part from `::first-letter`/`::first-line` pseudo element\r\n - remaining part, parent element\r\n\r\nIn step 4,\r\n>If node is a Text node, then for each CSS text box produced by node\r\n\r\nWe can read \"CSS text box produced by node\" are `::first-letter` /`::first-line` boxes and boxes from remaining part. It is OK to mention \"visibility\" for each CSS text box in step 4.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
