    "created_at": "2018-07-24T02:00:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-07-24T02:00:18Z",
    "body": ">That looks like a Blink implementation detail, isn't it?\r\n\r\nYes, this is Blink/WebKit implementation details. In Blink/WebKit, they have generated Text node inside first-letter pseudo element, e.g.\r\n``html\r\n<p>\r\n<p::first-letter>\r\n  <span>#Text node contains first-letter part\r\n</p::first-letter>\r\n#Text original text which contains both first-letter and remaining part\r\n``\r\nNote: For first-line, Blink/WebKit, they don't have pseudo element.\r\n\r\n> Text inside the first-letter is supposed to inherit from the first-letter.\r\nYes, that why term we need to change step 2 to make meaning of the term \"node\" clear.\r\n\r\nBTW, I filed the bug in Chromium bug tracker[1] to make Blink don't apply \"visibility\" to\r\nfirst-letter.\r\n\r\nEven if Blink do so, we should make the spec to mention about this to make the spec clear and help future browser implementers.\r\n\r\n[1] http://crbug.com/866744 ::first-letter should not apply \"visibility\" CSS property\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
